  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Help on the Way (multiple takes w/banter)** (1 other source): Several takes of Help on the Way flow into Slipknot!, with noodling between attempts [1]\n- **Slipknot! (demo playback) banter/dead air/banter** (1 review): Reviewer hears an apparent discontinuity after the Slipknot demo playback and doubts everything comes from one date [3]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **changes/banter (multiple takes)**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **Habanera/banter**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **changes/jam**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **changes/banter (multiple takes)**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **changes/banter (multiple takes)**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **jam/banter**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **jam/banter (multiple takes)**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **Blues for Allah/banter (multiple takes)**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [4]\n- Earliest performances in the archive: The Music Never Stopped (blues jam) [4]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **gd1975-03-01.145786.sbd.gans.miller.noel.flac1644** (recommended): soundboard; 35 songs; 459 min; rated 2.5/5 by 2 [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Garcia counts off takes aloud, and faint cheers are audible in the studio after an out-jam [1]\n- Later takes of Franklin's Tower appear, along with a tape rewind and stretches of just guitars and talk [1]\n- Reviewer says the casual studio chatter feels like eavesdropping on the band at work [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **gd1975-03-01.145786.sbd.gans.miller.noel.flac1644**: taped by David Gans; transferred by Joe Noel and Charlie Miller; source: Soundboard -> ? -> PCM [1]",
